    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_8732b575",
      "@type": "OverallIntent",
      "instance_name": "overallintent_instance",
      "label": "the overallintent",
      "description": "meme-id: dss; hasOverallIntent: Harmful; overall-intent-description: The image depicts a baby in a diaper standing in front of an open dishwasher, seemingly interacting with it. The text 'dss' is overlaid in the top-left corner. The overall intent of this meme is to humorously suggest that the baby is 'doing the dishes' — a play on the acronym 'dss' which stands for 'doing the dishes.' While the image itself is not inherently abusive, hateful, or misogynistic, the meme's humor relies on infantilizing the baby by implying it is capable of performing an adult task. This can be considered mildly harmful or inappropriate as it may reinforce stereotypes about children's capabilities or be seen as mocking the baby's innocence. The meme does not target any specific protected group, but its humor is derived from the absurdity of a baby engaging in a household chore, which may be perceived as infantilizing or demeaning to the child's perceived maturity. The intent is primarily comedic and relies on visual juxtaposition (baby + dishwasher) with the text 'dss' to create a pun-based joke.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_35c7dc57"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
